## Retention by month

data decay = months since signup,Jun,Jul,Aug,Sep; Month 0,100,100,100,100; Month 1,46,48,51,53; Month 2,38,40,43,; Month 3,33,35,,
chart line decay unit=% min=0 max=100 focus=Sep title="Share of each cohort still active"

Each newer cohort sits a little above the one before it at every month it has reached.

## Takeaways

1. The onboarding changes shipped on 2026-07-20 line up with the jump in month-1 retention from 48 percent (July) to 51 percent (August).
2. The biggest drop is always between month 0 and month 1, where every cohort loses roughly half its users.
3. September's cohort is the largest so far, at 29,800 new users, and also the best retaining, at 53 percent in month 1.
